This example creates a `CommentParser` class that can parse HTML strings and extract comments. It provides methods to append an HTML comment to the string, as well as to get the contents of a comment at a given position.

The `parse()` method uses a while loop to iterate over the HTML string and find all comments. Each comment is created by extracting its contents using the `getCommentContent()` method, which checks if the current position is within the start of a comment using the `isCommentStart()` method.

Once a comment has been found, it can be appended to the original HTML string using the `appendComment()` or `appendCommentAsFile()` methods. The resulting comments are stored in an array of `Comment` objects and returned by the `parse()` method.

In the example main function, we create a new parser with an initial HTML string containing only one comment. We then call the `parse()` method to extract all comments from the string, which are logged to the console.
